Janko


From janko.thyson at ku-eichstaett.de  Fri Sep 10 01:11:29 2010
From: janko.thyson at ku-eichstaett.de (Janko Thyson)
Date: Fri, 10 Sep 2010 01:11:29 +0200
Subject: [Roxygen-devel] Problems with roxygen and setMethod
Message-ID: <000b01cb5074$55850340$008f09c0$@thyson@ku-eichstaett.de>

Okay, I found the cause of the error:

This is the method def that didn't pass 'roxygenize()'

setMethod(f = "test.method", signature(self="MyClass"), 
    function(self, ...) {
        msg.fun.info(self = self)
        fun <- selectMethod(f = "test.method", signature = "ANY")
        mthds <- fun(self)
        return(mthds)
    })

This is the method def that did pass 'roxygenize()'

setMethod(f = "class.methods.get", signature(self="Shabubu_Hub"), 
    function(self, ...) {
        msg.fun.info(self = self)
        fun <- selectMethod(f = "class.methods.get", signature = c("ANY"))
        mthds <- fun(self)
        return(mthds)
    })

Regards,
Janko

