From laurent.gatto at gmail.com  Tue Sep 21 17:10:47 2010
From: laurent.gatto at gmail.com (Laurent Gatto)
Date: Tue, 21 Sep 2010 16:10:47 +0100
Subject: [Roxygen-devel] TODO tag error with Rd2
In-Reply-To: <AANLkTinDMugCmuV2aDS6Y1_S3VUbswNBb7=W3vvZTZPT@mail.gmail.com>
References: <AANLkTinDMugCmuV2aDS6Y1_S3VUbswNBb7=W3vvZTZPT@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <AANLkTimJPU_ve3g4jcEsQJ5YjSbZ3EG+CRb2JCZGEq=e@mail.gmail.com>

To fix this issue, I have modified function parse.todo in file Rd2.R

parse.todo <- function(key, value)
  append.Rd(todoTag(key,value))

And added a todoTag function to Rdapi.R

todoTag <- function(k,v)
  return(sectionTag('Todo',paste('{', v, '}')))

I am not sure if this issue was affecting other users and to what
extend this represent a reasonable fix, but it seems to work with a
couple examples I tries and produces the same results as
use.Rd2=FALSE.

Best wishes,

Laurent

